    {
      "source": "After an aggregate root gets saved (that is, inserted or updated).",
      "translation": "在聚合根被保存（即插入或更新）之后。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "Copyright © 2005 - <script>var d = new Date();\n        document.write(d.getFullYear());</script> Broadcom. All Rights Reserved. The term \"Broadcom\" refers to Broadcom Inc. and/or its subsidiaries.<br/><a href=\"https://www.vmware.com/help/legal.html\">Terms of Use</a> • <a href=\"https://www.vmware.com/help/privacy.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Privacy</a> • <a href=\"https://spring.io/trademarks\">Trademark Guidelines</a> <span id=\"thank-you-mobile\">• <a href=\"https://spring.io/thank-you\">Thank you</a></span> • <a href=\"https://www.vmware.com/help/privacy/california-privacy-rights.html\">Your California Privacy Rights</a> • <a class=\"ot-sdk-show-settings\">Cookie Settings</a> <span id=\"teconsent\"></span>",
      "translation": "版权所有 © 2005 - <script>var d = new Date(); document.write(d.getFullYear());</script> Broadcom。保留所有权利。“Broadcom”指 Broadcom Inc. 及其/或其子公司。<br/><a href=\"https://www.vmware.com/help/legal.html\">使用条款</a> • <a href=\"https://www.vmware.com/help/privacy.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">隐私政策</a> • <a href=\"https://spring.io/trademarks\">商标指南</a> <span id=\"thank-you-mobile\">• <a href=\"https://spring.io/thank-you\">致谢</a></span> • <a href=\"https://www.vmware.com/help/privacy/california-privacy-rights.html\">您的加州隐私权利</a> • <a class=\"ot-sdk-show-settings\">Cookie 设置</a> <span id=\"teconsent\"></span>",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "If you want to handle events only for a specific domain type you may derive your listener from <code>AbstractRelationalEventListener</code> and overwrite one or more of the <code>onXXX</code> methods, where <code>XXX</code> stands for an event type.\nCallback methods will only get invoked for events related to the domain type and their subtypes, therefore you don’t require further casting.",
      "translation": "如果您只想处理特定领域类型的事件，可以继承<code>AbstractRelationalEventListener</code>并重写一个或多个<code>onXXX</code>方法，其中<code>XXX</code>代表事件类型。回调方法将仅针对与该领域类型及其子类型相关的事件被调用，因此您无需进行进一步的类型转换。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Entity lifecycle events can be costly, and you may notice a change in the performance profile when loading large result sets.\nYou can disable lifecycle events on <code><a class=\"xref attachment apiref\" href=\"../api/java/org/springframework/data/jdbc/core/JdbcAggregateTemplate.html#setEntityLifecycleEventsEnabled(boolean)\">Template API</a></code>.",
      "translation": "实体生命周期事件可能会产生开销，在加载大型结果集时，您可能会注意到性能特征发生变化。您可以在 <code><a class=\"xref attachment apiref\" href=\"../api/java/org/springframework/data/jdbc/core/JdbcAggregateTemplate.html#setEntityLifecycleEventsEnabled(boolean)\">模板 API</a></code> 上禁用生命周期事件。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Spring Data JDBC uses the <a class=\"xref page\" href=\"../commons/entity-callbacks.html\"><code>EntityCallback</code> API</a> for its auditing support and reacts on the callbacks listed in the following table.",
      "translation": "Spring Data JDBC 使用<a class=\"xref page\" href=\"../commons/entity-callbacks.html\"><code>EntityCallback</code> API</a>来提供审计支持，并响应下表中列出的回调。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Spring Data JDBC publishes lifecycle events to <code>ApplicationListener</code> objects, typically beans in the application context.\nEvents are notifications about a certain lifecycle phase.\nIn contrast to entity callbacks, events are intended for notification.\nTransactional listeners will receive events when the transaction completes.\nEvents and callbacks get only triggered for aggregate roots.\nIf you want to process non-root entities, you need to do that through a listener for the containing aggregate root.",
      "translation": "Spring Data JDBC 将生命周期事件发布到 `<code>ApplicationListener</code>` 对象，通常是应用程序上下文中的 Bean。  \n事件是关于特定生命周期阶段的通知。  \n与实体回调不同，事件的目的是用于通知。  \n事务性监听器将在事务完成时接收事件。  \n事件和回调仅针对聚合根触发。  \n如果您需要处理非根实体，则需要通过包含该实体的聚合根的监听器来实现。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "The following table describes the available events. For more details about the exact relation between process steps see the <a href=\"#jdbc.entity-callbacks\">description of available callbacks</a> which map 1:1 to events.",
      "translation": "下表描述了可用的事件。有关进程步骤之间确切关系的更多详细信息，请参阅<a href=\"#jdbc.entity-callbacks\">可用回调的描述</a>，该描述与事件呈 1:1 映射关系。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "After an aggregate root gets created from a database <code>ResultSet</code> and all its properties get set.",
      "translation": "在从数据库的 `<code>ResultSet</code>` 创建聚合根并设置其所有属性之后。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Changes made to the aggregate root may get considered, but the decision if an id value will be sent to the database is already made in the previous step.\nDo not use this for creating Ids for new aggregates. Use <code>BeforeConvertCallback</code> instead.",
      "translation": "对聚合根所做的更改可能会被考虑，但是否将 ID 值发送到数据库的决策已在上一步骤中做出。请勿使用此方法为新聚合创建 ID，而应使用 `<code>BeforeConvertCallback</code>`。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "For example, the following listener gets invoked before an aggregate gets saved:",
      "translation": "例如，以下监听器会在聚合被保存之前被调用：",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Before an aggregate root gets deleted.",
      "translation": "在聚合根被删除之前。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "After an aggregate root gets deleted.",
      "translation": "在聚合根被删除后。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Before an aggregate root gets converted into a plan for executing SQL statements, but after the decision was made if the aggregate is new or not, i.e. if an update or an insert is in order.",
      "translation": "在将聚合根转换为执行 SQL 语句的计划之前，但在已决定该聚合是新增还是现有（即确定应执行更新还是插入操作）之后。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Before an aggregate root gets saved (that is, inserted or updated but after the decision about whether if it gets inserted or updated was made).",
      "translation": "在聚合根被保存之前（即，在决定是插入还是更新之后，但在实际执行插入或更新操作之前）。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Before the actual deletion.",
      "translation": "实际删除之前。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "The aggregate root and all the entities of that aggregate get removed from the database.",
      "translation": "聚合根及其所属聚合中的所有实体将从数据库中删除。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "After an aggregate gets deleted.",
      "translation": "在聚合被删除后。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Determine if an insert or an update of the aggregate is to be performed dependent on if it is new or not.",
      "translation": "根据聚合项是新还是已存在，确定是执行插入操作还是更新操作。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "This is the correct callback if you want to set an id programmatically. In the previous step new aggregates got detected as such and an Id generated in this step would be used in the following step.",
      "translation": "如果您希望通过编程方式设置 ID，这是正确的回调。在上一步中，新的聚合体已被识别并生成了 ID，本步骤生成的 ID 将在后续步骤中使用。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Convert the aggregate to an aggregate change, it is a sequence of SQL statements to be executed against the database. In this step the decision is made if an Id is provided by the aggregate or if the Id is still empty and is expected to be generated by the database.",
      "translation": "将聚合转换为聚合变更，即一系列针对数据库执行的 SQL 语句。在此步骤中，需决定是由聚合提供 ID，还是 ID 仍为空且预期由数据库生成。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "The SQL statements determined above get executed against the database.",
      "translation": "上述确定的 SQL 语句将在数据库中执行。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Load the aggregate using 1 or more SQL queries. Construct the aggregate from the resultset.",
      "translation": "使用一个或多个 SQL 查询加载聚合数据，并从结果集构建该聚合。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "We encourage the use of callbacks over events since they support the use of immutable classes and therefore are more powerful and versatile than events.",
      "translation": "我们鼓励使用回调而非事件，因为回调支持不可变类的用法，因此比事件更强大且功能更多样。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "The delete and save related callbacks do not get invoked for derived query methods or annotated queries.\nIn general Spring Data JDBC does not have an efficient way to determine what aggregates are affected by these operations and therefore can’t provide callbacks or events.",
      "translation": "删除和保存相关的回调不会在派生查询方法或注解查询中被调用。  \n一般来说，Spring Data JDBC 没有高效的方法来确定这些操作会影响哪些聚合，因此无法提供回调或事件。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
